Abstract = {A vegetation survey of natural grasslands was undertaken in the urban
   areas of Gauteng, supporting about 20\% of the country's population.
   Releves were compiled in 132 sample plots placed in selected open spaces
   in the study area. A floristic-sociological classification revealed
   eight grassland communities, represented by 59 releves. A hierarchical
   classification, description and ecological interpretation of these plant
   communities are presented. (c) 2006 SAAB. Published by Elsevier B.V. All
